  "plain": "This theory holds that the reported crash of an unknown craft near Roswell, New Mexico, in 1947 marks a dividing line, separating the spirits and strange beings of older folklore from the 'aliens' people have described since. Michels says it is the theory he likes best, and credits it to the researcher Jacques Vallée and the religious studies scholar Diana Pasulka, in a 2021 episode with the Stanford scientist Garry Nolan. If true, it would mean the same phenomenon has always been with us and only changed its face in 1947."
